PN,30918
SC,0018
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786468725
OL,3,CSolar eclipse UK: When and where to
OL,4,Cwatch the rare celestial phenomenon
OL,6,FA double treat for skywatchers
OL,8,FAs if one spectacular celestial event
OL,9,Fwasn't enough, the Perseid meteor
OL,10,Fshower will also peak on the night of
OL,11,FAugust 12 to 13.
OL,13,FWith the Moon in its new phase
OL,14,Ffollowing the eclipse, skies will be
OL,15,Fbeautifully dark, providing ideal
OL,16,Fconditions for spotting shooting stars.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G18/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30919
SC,0019
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786468725
OL,3,CSolar eclipse UK: When and where to
OL,4,Cwatch the rare celestial phenomenon
OL,6,FUnder clear, dark skies, observers
OL,7,Fcould see 20-40 meteors per hour
OL,8,Facross much of the UK, with even
OL,9,Fhigher rates possible in areas free
OL,10,Ffrom light pollution.
OL,12,FThe best time to watch will be after
OL,13,Fmidnight and into the early hours of
OL,14,FThursday morning, when the
OL,15,Fconstellation of Perseus climbs higher
OL,16,Finto the sky.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G19/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
